WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:07.750
Part eleven: admin levels. Choose what each admin can do: Viewer, Coordinator, Manager, or Full.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:14.275
In the Hub spreadsheet, on the Lists tab, the Admin level column sits next to Portal admins.

00:00:14.475 --> 00:00:19.233
Pick each admin's level on the same row as their email or Person ID.

00:00:19.433 --> 00:00:26.282
Viewer, Coordinator, Manager, or Full. A blank is Full, so admins added before levels keep everything.

00:00:26.482 --> 00:00:30.970
A change counts on their very next tap. No new sign-in needed.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:33.698
The brown bar shows your level.

00:00:33.898 --> 00:00:44.620
A Viewer can look up volunteers, see the stands and every roster, use the directory, and send group texts. Nothing they see can be changed, and there are no Hub tools.

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:51.231
On a roster, a Viewer sees every name and number, with no Move, Hand off, or Remove buttons.

00:00:51.431 --> 00:00:54.040
The group text buttons still work.

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:58.069
A Coordinator can also make the everyday changes.

00:00:58.269 --> 00:01:01.043
Send stand sheets, and add a worker by hand.

00:01:01.243 --> 00:01:07.068
Open stand time sheets, and act for a volunteer: their paperwork page, or naming their spots.

00:01:07.268 --> 00:01:15.190
Add, move, hand off, and remove people on Hub rosters. Adding someone with missing paperwork still takes a Manager.

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:23.465
A Manager can also review paperwork, approve stand logs, decide no-shows, and answer family manager requests.

00:01:23.665 --> 00:01:26.609
Plus cancel a stand or game, and Manage stands.

00:01:26.809 --> 00:01:29.434
Full can do everything, including Hub health.

00:01:29.634 --> 00:01:35.470
The Hub checks the level on every request, so hiding a button is never the only lock.
